    ('Nov 2026', "OPEN YY's Seoul Fall/Winter 2026; leather on the ramp in Kolkata", "Korean label OPEN YY presented a loose, draped FW26 collection on 2 November: hooded fur coats and fur bombers, wired peacoats, shearling-trimmed skirts, leather trousers and jersey and knit dresses meant to be layered and mixed. In Kolkata, the Indian Leather Products Association's 'Leather on the Ramp' (29 October, reported 3 November) styled bags from NS Leather, Trio, Gioia by D2 and Vabadus with fusion skirts and sarees.", [('Pause', 'https://pausemag.co.uk/2026/11/open-yy-presents-seoul-inspired-fall-winter-2026-collection/'), ('t2online', 'https://t2online.in/events/events-1/ilpa-presents-leather-on-the-ramp-2026--with-t2--showcased-a-sleek-and-stylish-range-of-accessories/2008985')]),
    ('Nov 2026', 'Dubai: AFC Fashion Fund Emirati Chapter; Zuhair Murad x ALDO evening capsule; Louis Vuitton holiday pop-up in Shibuya', "The Arab Fashion Council named Amina Taher as its new chair and unveiled the AFC Fashion Fund Emirati Chapter on 4 November at Maison Revka, Delano Dubai, offering selected Emirati designers mentorship, retail access and international exposure. Lebanese couturier Zuhair Murad's capsule with ALDO launched on 4 November: a sculptural block-heel platform sandal and a pointed-toe slingback pump in glitter, metallic gold and snakeskin-effect finishes, plus evening bags with statement hardware and pearl jewellery. Louis Vuitton's train-station holiday 2026 campaign opens an immersive pop-up in Shibuya, Tokyo on 7 November.", [('Mille World', 'https://www.milleworld.com/the-week-in-chic-all-the-fashion-news-you-might-have-missed-oct-31-nov-06/')]),
    ('Nov 2026', 'Singapore openings at 313@somerset; Margiela x Gentle Monster pop-ups; Café Lacoste in Seoul', "Vietnamese label Lsoul opened its first Singapore flagship at 313@somerset with its fall/winter 2026 collection, and Gentlewoman opened its first Singapore store in the same mall in October. Maison Margiela and Gentle Monster are taking their eyewear collaboration to pop-ups in four Asian cities; Fila Fusion opened an OOTidol pop-up in Shanghai, Dsquared2 opened a boutique at The Londoner Macau and Lacoste opened Asia's first Café Lacoste in Seoul.", [("Harper's Bazaar Singapore", 'https://harpersbazaar.com.sg/fashion/news-trends/all-fashion-news-you-need-know-right-now'), ('Jing Daily', 'https://jingdaily.com/')]),
    ('Oct 2026', 'Musinsa deepens its tie-up with Japan\'s Zozo ahead of a 2027 IPO', "Zozo opened its first South Korean pop-up inside a Musinsa store in Seoul on 16 October, selling 15 Japanese brands through the end of October, and Musinsa sells Zozo products online until mid-November. Musinsa has applied to list on the Korea Exchange, targeting the first half of 2027, and plans its first permanent store in Japan in 2027.", [('KrASIA / Nikkei Asia', 'https://kr-asia.com/south-korean-fashion-platform-musinsa-deepens-ties-with-japans-zozo-ahead-of-ipo')]),
    ('Oct 2026', 'Buttonscarves "Pleats Me" at Jakarta Fashion Week 2027', "On 30 October at City Hall, Pondok Indah Mall 3, Buttonscarves (creative director Miftahul Jannah) showed 'Pleats Me', 26 looks with pleats as the main element of every design, inspired by the lines of fossil dunes; its first full collection built on pleating. Looks included blue pleats and a red-and-black gown with feather trim worn by Luna Maya. Elsewhere in the week Ivan Gunawan showed black and white and Studio Tui dark colours.", [('IDN Times', 'https://www.idntimes.com/life/women/buttonscarves-eksplorasi-pleats-di-jfw-2027-00-m7q22-s15d8n'), ('IDN Times (artists on the runway)', 'https://www.idntimes.com/hype/entertainment/artis-tampil-di-jakarta-fashion-week-2027-memesona-di-runway-00-sd4vv-v1ctjj')]),
    ('Oct 2026', 'Dubai: Chloé opens at Atlantis The Royal; Piaget high jewellery at Jumeirah', "Chloé (creative director Chemena Kamali) opened a boutique at Atlantis The Royal, Palm Jumeirah, on 30 October, including a 'Chloé à la Plage' offer of breezy silhouettes and broderie anglaise. Piaget showed 'Colours of Extraleganza', more than 150 high-jewellery pieces with emeralds, rubies, sapphires, opals, tiger's eye and mother-of-pearl, at L'Ambassade villa in Jumeirah until 31 October.", [('Mille World', 'https://www.milleworld.com/the-week-in-chic-all-the-fashion-news-you-might-have-missed-oct-23-30/')]),
    ('Oct 2026', 'Jakarta Fashion Week 2027: woven heritage on the main stage', "At City Hall, Pondok Indah Mall 3 (26 Oct–1 Nov, 111 designers), Chitra Subyakto's Sejauh Mata Memandang showed loose long dresses, long-sleeve tops and layered sets in white, ivory, cream, pale pink, brown, black and blue with cat motifs, while DARRA reworked Javanese lurik, ikat, batik and songket into tunics and ankle-length overlayers with multi-direction stripes and matching hoods (27 Oct). Cita Tenun Indonesia's 'TEXTUM' show set Cual Bangka ikat with gold or silver sungkit inlay (Priyo Oktaviano), Dayak weaving (Wilsen Willim) and the revived Inuh weave of Lampung (Eri Dani) on the main stage.", [('CNN Indonesia', 'https://www.cnnindonesia.com/gaya-hidup/20261028083141-277-1420407/motif-kucing-hingga-isu-karhutla-warnai-koleksi-di-jfw-2027'), ('Republika', 'https://ameera.republika.co.id/berita/tnnnio328/cti-bawa-tenun-cual-bangka-dayak-iban-dan-inuh-lampung-ke-jfw-2027'), ('Kumparan', 'https://kumparan.com/kumparanwoman/foto-jakarta-fashion-week-2027-resmi-dibuka-tampilkan-karya-111-desainer-28SHyLuFuse')]),
    ('Oct 2026', 'Maison Margiela x Gentle Monster: fourth eyewear collaboration', "Launched 29 October with 43 sunglasses and 25 optical frames: oversized shields, crushed and reconstructed shapes and narrow upswept frames wrapped in leather, with Margiela's four white stitches made to appear to float on the frame. Pop-ups run in eight cities including Seoul, Tokyo and Shanghai, with a performance in Seoul.", [('Mille World', 'https://www.milleworld.com/the-week-in-chic-all-the-fashion-news-you-might-have-missed-oct-23-30/')]),
    ('Oct 2026', 'Festive menswear and mirror-work lehengas in Delhi', "Kriti Sanon closed Abhinav Mishra's 'Into the Wild 2026' show on 24 October at Mehar Villas, New Delhi, in a black mirror-work lehenga with hand embroidery, metallic embellishment and horse motifs, an embellished bralette blouse and a sheer sequinned dupatta.", [('t2online', 'https://t2online.in/goodlife/fashion-beauty/abhinav-mishra-unveils-into-the-wild-2026--with-kriti-sanon-as-showstopper/2008837'), ('Sentinel Assam', 'https://www.sentinelassam.com/more-news/entertainment/kriti-sanon-turns-showstopper-at-abhinav-mishras-into-the-wild-2026')]),
    ('Oct 2026', 'Tarun Tahiliani closes Dubai Fashion Week SS27', "On 26 October Tarun Tahiliani closed the week with 'The Many Moods of TT', mixing Indian craft with Middle Eastern couture ahead of his first Dubai store. Looks included structured tunics with wide-leg trousers, cape dresses, kaftans, layered robes and long jackets, scarf-like panels, mandarin collars and tassels, in sunset shades of mustard, orange, bronze, crimson and burgundy. Singer Maya Diab closed in an embellished silver lehenga with a sheer dupatta.", [('Free Press Journal', 'https://www.freepressjournal.in/lifestyle/lebanese-singer-maya-diab-turns-desi-showstopper-in-dazzling-lehenga-for-tarun-tahilianis-dubai-fashion-show'), ('Gulf News', 'https://gulfnews.com/the-kurator/the-kurators-dubai-fashion-week-ss27-round-up-1.500725939')]),
    ('Oct 2026', 'Jakarta Fashion Week 2027 opens: "City of New Lights"', 'The week runs 26 October to 1 November 2026 at City Hall, Pondok Indah Mall 3, with 111 designers. A SEA WAVES programme with Indonesia\'s Ministry of Tourism, "Two Expressions of Southeast Asian Heritage", shows installations and exhibitions on traditional crafts and Southeast Asian woven textiles. Competitions for fashion, menswear and accessory designers run alongside the Dewi Luxe Market. Day one (26 October) featured new collections from local labels Vaia and MKS+ and the LPPM Menswear emerging-designer competition.', [('Fimela', 'https://www.fimela.com/fashion/read/8314552/soroti-warisan-tekstil-asia-tenggara-jakarta-fashion-week-2027-hadir-dengan-tema-city-of-new-lights'), ('Wolipop (detik)', 'https://wolipop.detik.com/fashion-news/d-8707309/bersiap-jakarta-fashion-week-2027-bakal-diramaikan-111-desainer'), ('Scarf Media', 'https://www.scmedia.id/jakarta-fashion-week-2027-hari-pertama-intip-koleksi-terbaru-brand-fashion-lokal/')]),
    ('Oct 2026', 'Dubai Fashion Week SS27 days 2–3: sporty daywear, crystals and Colombia Day', 'Nafsika Skourti closed day two with "Sisters by Choice": light, sporty daywear with ribbon-trimmed sleeves and skirts, woven-beaded open-back tops, roomy floral skirts and zip-through tops. Yousef Al Jasmi showed crystal-encrusted, body-skimming dresses moving from nude to black; Sara Pedram showed wing-like shoulders, a burnt-amber paillette column and a Prussian-blue velvet gown. Kresha Bajaj put beadwork on crochet tops and tanks. Day three (25 October) was Colombia Day (see South America). In the showroom: 3D-printed bags from Bahrain\'s Touchless and trench and tuxedo jackets with porcelain buttons from Kuwait\'s Kochylia.', [('The National', 'https://www.thenationalnews.com/lifestyle/fashion-beauty/2026/10/25/dubai-fashion-week-2026/'), ('A&E Magazine', 'https://aeworld.com/fashion/colombian-designers-take-centre-stage-on-day-three-of-dubai-fashion-week-ss27/')]),
    ('Oct 2026', 'Dubai Fashion Week SS27: couture craft leads the opening', "Opening-day shows on 23 October leaned on handwork: Kuwaiti designer Yousef AlJasmi debuted in black, cream and silver; Sara Pedram's Simorgh collection used hand embroidery and hand-painted florals; Indian designer Pallavi Puri showed 50 couture looks made by more than 150 artisans; and Krésha Bajaj with Alok Lodha Jewels showed beadwork and painterly florals. A month-long Harvey Nichols pop-up (1–31 October) sells regional labels alongside the week.", [('Dubai PR Network', 'https://www.dubaiprnetwork.com/fashion-news/194653-highlights-from-opening-day-of-dubai-fashion-week-ss27'), ('Al-Monitor', 'https://www.al-monitor.com/newsletter/2026-10-23/dubai-steps-back-runway')]),
    ('Oct 2026', 'Lakmē Fashion Week x FDCI (Delhi): black, gold and draped festive menswear', "The 13–18 October edition in Delhi mixed bridal illusion and deep black. Namrata Joshipura's OBSIDIAN used black with metallic finishes, gold embroidery and her long jumpsuits; Anushree Reddy layered zardozi, sequins and glass beads; Ashish N Soni worked Arvind cotton, wool, linen, Tencel and bamboo, with looks sold at The Arvind Stores; Suneet Varma's Kashi showed draped saris and dhoti skirts in red, purple, maroon and black; Tasva paired an angrakha-style tunic, bandhgala and pre-draped doshala.", [('Outlook Luxe (Day 4)', 'https://luxe.outlookindia.com/fashion-beauty/couture/lakme-fashion-week-x-fdci-2026-day-4-namrata-joshipura-anushree-reddy-and-ashish-n-soni-lead-the-line-up'), ('Outlook Luxe', 'https://luxe.outlookindia.com/amp/story/fashion-beauty/couture/lakme-fashion-week-x-fdci-2026-suneet-varmas-kashi-samant-chauhans-jaisalmer-and-more')]),
    ('Oct 2026', "China's Double 11 opens with direct discounts", 'Tmall pre-sales opened on 15 October with official sales from 20 October; JD.com started on 12 October and dropped deposit pre-sales; Douyin\'s festival runs 15 October to 11 November. Tmall reports about 1 million brands taking part and favours straight discounts over cross-store thresholds, after a 10 October government notice on "lowest price" practices. Activewear label ALO, which opened on Tmall in August, has its first major China promotion.', [('BigGo Finance', 'https://finance.biggo.com/news/b8682e59-edaa-48da-8f8b-3a383cd2008a')]),
    ('Oct 2026', 'Dubai Fashion Week SS27 opens; Tarun Tahiliani to close', 'The SS27 edition opened on 22 October at Dubai Design District with Paris-based Ludovic de Saint Sernin and Kuwaiti designer Yousef Al Jasmi. The schedule includes Nafsika Skourti, Weinsanto, Lebanese label Lili Blanc and Emirati debut labels Onori and Kuni. Indian designer Tarun Tahiliani closes on 26 October and is opening a Jumeirah boutique, his first outside India.', [('The National', 'https://www.thenationalnews.com/lifestyle/fashion-beauty/2026/10/21/dubai-fashion-week-returns-with-ludovic-de-saint-sernin-tarun-tahiliani-and-regional-talent/'), ('Gulf News', 'https://gulfnews.com/lifestyle/fashion/tarun-tahiliani-weinsanto-nafsika-skourti-day-by-day-guide-to-dubai-fashion-week-1.500719365')]),
    ('Oct 2026', 'Jakarta Fashion Week 2027 opens 26 October', 'Indonesia\'s main fashion week runs 26 October to 1 November 2026 in Jakarta, with a model search and BTN Fashion Lab linking designers with small businesses (UMKM) and local artisans.', [('Indonesia Travel', 'https://www.indonesia.travel/au-en/events/event-detail/jfw-2027')]),
    ('Oct 2026', 'Shanghai Fashion Week SS27: "Renewed Radiance"', 'Nearly 100 runway presentations and about 1,000 brands. HEMU opened with Dunhuang heritage techniques (yunjin and song brocade, kesi silk tapestry, embroidery); the season spotlights traditional Chinese motifs inspired by the Silk Road.', [('China Daily', 'https://www.chinadaily.com.cn/a/202609/23/WS6ab3e914e4b06d4aa055fd84.html'), ('CGTN', 'https://news.cgtn.com/news/2026-10-09/Spring-Summer-2027-Shanghai-Fashion-Week-kicks-off--1R6bkJ10QTK/p.html')]),
    ('Oct 2026', 'Dubai Fashion Week SS27 widens its map', 'Running 22–26 October at Dubai Design District, with designers from the UAE, Kuwait, India, Colombia, Vietnam, Ukraine, Azerbaijan, Jordan, France and Italy, and a buyers\' programme for regional and international stores.', [('Dubai PR Network', 'https://www.dubaiprnetwork.com/fashion-news/194513-dubai-fashion-week-announces-spring-summer-2027-edition-programme')]),
    ('Sep 2026', 'Seoul SS27: tailoring as a system', 'Kwaeja-inspired overlapping forms, cropped jackets and windbreakers, ballooning trousers; earth tones with sheer fabrics and metallic silver; technical fabrics and denim-effect patchwork.', [('METAL Magazine', 'https://metalmagazine.eu/en/post/seoul-fashion-week-ss-2027-our-favourite-collections')]),
    ('Sep 2026', 'Tokyo SS27: translucency and reworked office wear', 'Yoshiokubo layered translucent fabrics with utility thermals; Pillings twisted shirts and pencil skirts with off-centre creases; Charinyeh used gossamer fabrics and coral-like cut jacquard.', [('Tokyo Weekender', 'https://www.tokyoweekender.com/art_and_culture/fashion/rakuten-fashion-week-tokyo-ss-2027-designers/')]),
